{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556879-new-tremere-house-house-zmei","id":1556879,"title":"New Tremere House: House Zmei","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-12-21T14:36:47-08:00","id":1556879,"title":"New Tremere House: House Zmei","content":"I quite like the mythology surrounding the Tremere\u2014their relationship with the draconic symbols used by the Orders and with their Dragon itself is very interesting. I was somewhat disappointed, however, by the lack of integration of these draconic themes with the rest of their kit. I have several dragon-themed mages seeking truths about what happened to them in my Chronicle, including mysteries surrounding souls and past lives, so I thought the Tremere would make perfect antagonists to act as a foil.<br /> <br /> Thusly, I've constructed a House which plays up on some of the things I'd like to explore with the Order. I'll be using it in my game for an NPC rival, but I think it would work well for player characters as well in the right circumstances since, like with House Vedmak, it can be used for protective purposes.<br /> <br /> Edit: I've added a new mechanical backing to the Tasting and updated the optional Attainments to better reflect the Fated aspects of the House.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:24px\">House Zmei</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Nicknames:</b> Dragons, Rulers, Serpents<br /> <br /> Throughout the Slavic lands, tales of dragons have always persisted. The great zmei standing at the flaming entrance to the underworld, the Chuda-Yuda living in the Black Sea beyond the waters none of the living may reach, the trickster-serpent god residing at the roots of the world tree \u2014 these stories and more survive even through sleeping eyes, visions of irrevocable truth. In the lands of Croatia and Slovenia, folk told of the pozoj dwelling beneath human civilization, great and terrible beasts who could shake the earth with a mere shrug. Only the students of black arts could banish them, as the tale goes, and so the students did.<br /> <br /> The so-called black school students came not to fight, however, but to know. Chasing every shard of knowledge, they sought to unravel the Great Mystery of the Dragons \u2014 the truest beings of magic, vanished in all but bones and symbols. Above and below, ephemera and flesh, bound and unbound they searched, spoke, claimed, until reaching the ultimate truth: the true Dragon was within. Within each and every soul, ignited by the inheritance of awakening, all souls follow the tree roots back to the serpent. And so did the founder find what he sought, blossoming as a true Dragon anew. But, in doing so, he summoned his own bogatyr \u2014 the Tremere, the blade-wielding hero, the golden spear of St. George which brings the dragons to heel.<br /> <br /> The dragon had long foreseen it. The dragon had welcomed it. As that spear pierce his heart, so he was devoured \u2014 and so he devoured. The slayer as the slain, the slain as the slayer, the Ouroboros ate itself. But, in returning to his own coils, he was born anew. What walked free from there was no longer human, for he never was.<br /> <br /> Or so goes the tale the dragons tell. Like the origins of the Tremere itself, the truth is endlessly debated and obscured \u2014 twisting with strange prose and unknown secrets. Those dragons who become known often face persecution from others of the Order, their claims of allegiance to the Seventh Dragon thrown into question with their tendency to feast on blood as well as soul and their monstrous, inhuman forms. Such is the burden they must bear, monsters among monsters \u2014 dragons amongst dragons.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Origins and Doctrine</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> Prospective dragons do not seek the House \u2014 it seeks them. The backgrounds members come from are as varied as the Slavic folktales it hearkens back to, but all are united by a single, unidentifiable <i>itch </i>beneath the flesh. The Seventh Dragon is no mere symbolic parlance or untouchable ideal to them, but as real, tangible, and <i>present</i> as the Tremere know all things. The Zmei's obsessions with draconity vary in nature: from pursuit of the Atlantean mystery to the pervasive desire to be dragons themselves. For all, joining the House is the only way to fulfill their true calling. For many, feeling the cool black scales tear apart their flesh the only way find true relief.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> Those of the House are singularly defined by their weakness, what they call the true Dragon's claim upon their form. Curiously, such weakness is directly tied to their level of Hollow enlightenment. It usually begins with the emergence of scales along their thighs, shoulders, and the small of their backs, eyes taking on a strange glow and narrowing pupil. Sharpening fangs and claws often come next, with more extreme alterations are not far behind. Tails, wild manes, and bodies more than half covered in scale are not uncommon by the time most reach the Disciple Attainment, what happens beyond this point remaining a mystery even to those of the House.<br /> <br /> Only those who purposefully keep their Hollow rating low may hide their draconic traits without the use of magic, specially designed clothing quickly becoming a necessity for those of higher Hollow seeking to stay decent and comfortable. By that time, of course, most will have carefully crafted illusory personas \u2014 but none can resist the temptation to be free from even that forever. All tend to keep well-groomed to the point of vanity, the outfits, be they physical or a trick of the Arcana, tending towards the regal and imposing \u2014 the spitting image of draconic royalty in human form.<br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Death 2, Destiny 3, Strength 3, Presence 3, an Obsession related to Dragons<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation:</b> The initiate must find a magic item, supernatural being, or other potent phenomena representative of draconic power and claim it for their own \u2014 either by devouring it, absorbing it, or otherwise taking it within themselves. Some practice Spirit magic to find those elemental forces of the land shaped into draconic form; others practice Mind magic to find powerful cultural representations of dragons in the Temenous or the imagined dragons of potent dreamers in their Oneiros. Others without such skills summon Supernal beings to help fulfill their purpose, taking their magic or bargaining for Artifacts.<br /> <br /> <b>Organization: </b>The House has no central leadership, each mentor-student bond a story of its own. Elder dragons often seek prospective members through dreams to avoid drawing unnecessary attention or leaving their lairs, walking through the Oneiroi of stolen souls as great black dragons. House members are expected to form domains of their own called Provinces, their Attainments helping them in monitoring their subjects against supernatural incursion and keeping such forces under their control. Because of this, they are often more open to working with other supernaturals than the standard Tremere, allowing them to operate in the same spaces in harmony \u2014 so long as they serve under the dragon's rulership and threaten not the subjects rightfully theirs. Vampires, however, remain an exception to this goodwill, the Damned acting as near direct rivals to the House's way of life.<br /> <br /> <b>Theory:</b> Zmei seek the torn pieces of the Final Watchtower in more than just souls. In claiming the Flesh and and Blood once lost to their great father, they believe the true Dragon may be made whole once more. By serving this purpose and embodying draconic strength wholly and truly, they know they paint a mystical target on their back \u2014 but they know only they can make that sacrifice, and thus they know they are the Seventh Dragon's most favored children.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Magic</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Yantras: </b>Incorporating draconic imagery or themes (+1); casting from dangerous or remote areas (+1, +2 if in a realm invisible); devouring a heart (+1 if animal, +2 if human, +3 if supernatural); breaking weapons or tools traditionally used in dragon slaying (+1, +2 if magical); displaying the house weakness to others (+2).<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Getting service from Province subjects; practicing physical skills using traits gained from the house weakness; eating large and extravagant meals; meditating into the Astral or entering another's dreams through a taken soul.<br /> <br /> <b>Weakness:</b> As a dragon's Hollow increases, their body manifests greater and more potent draconic traits. For every 3 points of Hollow a dragon possesses (rounded up), they must choose a new physical feature as in the spell Transform Life (Mage, p. 150) to represent the dragon tearing free from their flesh. These features must be commonly associated with dragons: horns, claws, fangs, gills, scaly armor, wings, and extrasensory perceptions the most applicable options. These features may not be physically removed, such as through transformation spells, and they will magically shred any clothing attempting to physically cover them. They may be magically obscured, but doing so comes at a cost: a dragon may not regain Willpower through their Vice in a scene unless they have &quot;shown off&quot; their draconic traits to at least one human subject.<br /> <br /> Additionally, taking on the mantle of the dragon warps the Zmei's guiding Destiny to match. Their Doom becomes &quot;die at the hands of a dragon slayer&quot; if it was not already.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Attainments</b></span><br /> <br /> House Zmei's Attainments often rely on what they call the &quot;Tasting.&quot; The dragon must either devour the flesh, drink the blood, or taste the soul of a target to place them under their metaphysical ownership. In addition to acting as a prerequisite for certain Attainment effects, the tasting acts as a substitute for their Duration factor \u2014 more difficult and intimate methods offering longer lasting effects. See the chart below for example Tasting times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"left\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Tasting Method</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Requirements</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Duration</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Glancing Taste</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Must touch target or succeed on a touch attack in combat.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1 Scene/1 Hour</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Biting in Combat</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Deal at least one point of damage from a bite grapple maneuver.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1 Chapter/1 Day</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Drinking Blood</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Must succeed on a Hold grapple maneuver or keep extracted blood transplant-viable.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3 Chapters/1 Week</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Ritualistically Consuming Flesh</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Spend at least one Ritual interval as defined by Hollow consuming flesh.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1 Story/1 Month</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Replacing a Soul with a Spent Soul</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">The swapped soul must have been fully drained by the dragon themselves.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3 Stories/6 Months</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Holding an Empty Vessel's Soul</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Must use a personal hollowstone or soul jar effect and the target must stay soulless.</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Indefinite</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> Many dragons find themselves setting up elaborate social mechanisms within their Provinces to ensure the subjects they hoard stay under their claim, such as keeping a collective blood pool of their subjects preserved with Death magic from which they can sup on. While the keeping of soulless thralls from which a dragon's magic can work on indefinitely is tempting, many prefer the veil of secrecy which comes from causing no seeming ill effects to their subjects.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Apprentice Attainment: The Dragon's Claim</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Initiation<br /> <br /> To truly stake their claim, a dragon must guard their subjects with zealous passion. The dragon may remotely monitor the subjects they have Tasted, placing them under the effects of both the Death 1 spell <i>Soul Marks</i> (Mage, p. 128) and Fate 1 spell <i>Interconnections</i> (Mage, p. 135) with Reach applied to to the latter allowing for the monitoring of possession, supernatural mind control, and alterations of destiny. Any time a major change occurs in the factors monitored by these effects, the dragon will be alerted to it, and what has changed, regardless of distance. They automatically receive knowledge of what subject has been affected, but not what caused it.<br /> <br /> The dragon may keep a maximum number of subjects under the effects of this Attainment equal to their max Mana, as defined by their Hollow rating. The dragon may reflexively remove any subject affected by this Attainment, but doing so cuts the ties of metaphysical ownership \u2014 requiring another Tasting before they can be affected again.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional: </b>Fate 2<br /> <br /> Only the worthy may know the presence of the dragon, all attempts to reveal the monster before the tale calls for it fought against by the tides of fate. All attempts to track, trace, or unveil the dragon or their magical effects are penalized by their dots in Fate \u2014 including all spells utilizing Sympathetic links. This penalty may be ignored for a roll if a character uses the Destiny Merit to grant it the Rote action or to reroll it.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Disciple Attainment: The Dragon's Due</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Death 3, Destiny 4<br /> <br /> To embrace the dragon is to receive strength unbounded, but the dragon will always have its due. The dragon may bind a subject they have Tasted to an agreement, emulating the effects of the Fate 3 spell <i>Sworn Oaths</i> (Mage, p. 137) with Reach assigned for instant use. Rather than granting a Boon, however, the target gains an effective number of dots (or additional dots) in the Destiny merit equal to the dragon's own Destiny dots for the Duration of this effect. Regardless if they possessed a Destiny rating before, their Doom changes to match the House weakness as well.<br /> <br /> Rather than inflicting a Hex, too, the dragon instead gains the ability to reflexively devour the target upon their breaking of the agreement. This emulates the Death 3 spell <i>Devouring the Slain</i> (Mage, p. 130) with an additional amount of Potency equal to the dragon's Death dots. This effect does not require the target to be damaged and does not count towards the limit of times per day the dragon can gain Mana through Scouring.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional: </b>Fate 3<br /> <br /> The Hollow dragon may remove the very heart of their being, separating themselves from the spear of destiny which may pierce it. The dragon may inflict 3 points of lethal damage upon themselves to remove their own beating heart, pumping their blood still through the Sympathetic strings of fate. While the heart remains outside their body, they gain the constant effects of Fate Mage Armor with no need to activate it, stacking with other forms of Mage Armor (but not another instance of Fate armor), and they no longer suffer ill effect from avoiding their Doom.<br /> <br /> Performing this ritual comes at a cost, however \u2014 should the heart be destroyed, the dragon suffers 3 resistant points of aggravated damage as their body must work to reform a new heart. In addition, the heart possesses a Connected sympathetic link which, when used as a Yantra, automatically bypasses the penalty imposed by the optional Fate 2 effect of &quot;The Dragon's Claim.&quot;<br /> <br /> Some say these hearts persist even after the dragon's death, offering to pass on the cycle of slayer and slain. A Tremere with a House Attainment opportunity who devours such a heart may gain entry to the House for the cost of one Arcane Experience as normal.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Adept Attainment: The Dragon's Presence</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Death 4, Destiny 5<br /> <br /> To face the dragon is to face death, the incarnation of Creation's truest hunger. The dragon assumes the full form of their namesake, the great black-scaled serpent which brings all who face it under heel. This emulates the Death 4 spell Shadow Flesh (Mage, p. 132) with Reach assigned for instant use, but with the following changes.<br /> <br /> The dragon must choose the &quot;three-dimensional&quot; shadow option, taking on a draconic shape with all House weakness traits. They gain an amount of temporary Size equal to their dots in Death plus their dots in Hollow, though and they may not reduce their form or act as fluid shadow enough to move through cracks and crevices. They may still cast Supernal magic as normal, but they may also take physical actions against those they have Tasted.<br /> <br /> While using this Attainment, may make bite attacks as a lethal weapon with a modifier equal to half their Death dots, rounded up. This attack may be used even on subjects the dragon has not rendered &quot;physical&quot; to them yet, opening the subject up to further attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Optional:</b> Fate 4<br /> <br /> To slay the dragon is to become it, to devour and be devoured. A mage character who deals the killing blow to the dragon suffers a curse emulating the effects of the Fate 4spell <i>Divine Intervention </i>(Mage, p. 138). If the character does not possess Hollow, the Aspiration is &quot;undergo the Hollowing.&quot; Once a character fulfills this Aspiration, or if the character already possesses Hollow, the Aspiration becomes &quot;enter House Zmei.&quot; Failure to follow either Aspiration during a 24 hour period, rather than inflicting a Hex, inflicts an effect emulating the <i>Soulless </i>Condition (bypassing Tremere immunity) for the next day and counts as an Act of Hubris for Falling Wisdom.<br /> <br /> Should the slain dragon have removed their heart using the Fate 3 effect of &quot;The Dragon's Due,&quot; the victim <i>additionally </i>gains the Aspiration of &quot;find the dragon's heart.&quot; Should they fulfill this Aspiration, it changes to &quot;devour the dragon's heart when ready to enter House Zmei.&quot;<br /> <br /> This curse may only be removed by effects such as the Fate 4 spell <i>Atonement </i>(Mage, p. 138), wherein it counts as a Major curse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28963,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28963-wulfra","user":"Wulfra","date":". 12-22-2025, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28963-wulfra","name":"Wulfra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-21T20:16:13-08:00","id":1556890,"title":"","content":"I really like the concept, the symbolism of the dragon becoming an ouroboros is great as well, a metaphor for the Tremere's endless hunger. I aso really like the idea of the dragon's hoard being enforced by Fate. I think the House is thematically closer to Death primary and Fate secondary, rather than Prime optional.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Attainments, while they have instant use, they do not have advanced duration, so ones like the <i>Interconnections</i> and <i>Sworn Oaths</i> would only last a few turns.<br /> <br /> Lastly, Tremere Houses have a focus on utilizing the power of souls, I think it needs to be reflected more mechanically. If I understood correctly, Death embodies the dragon's hunger, and Fate their regal ferocity. I think it could be interesting if you build upon tasting souls and incorporated it more in the Attainments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-22T09:55:06-08:00","id":1556912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1556879-new-tremere-house-house-zmei?p=1556890#post1556890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the concept, the symbolism of the dragon becoming an ouroboros is great as well, a metaphor for the Tremere's endless hunger. I aso really like the idea of the dragon's hoard being enforced by Fate. I think the House is thematically closer to Death primary and Fate secondary, rather than Prime optional.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Attainments, while they have instant use, they do not have advanced duration, so ones like the <i>Interconnections</i> and <i>Sworn Oaths</i> would only last a few turns.<br /> <br /> Lastly, Tremere Houses have a focus on utilizing the power of souls, I think it needs to be reflected more mechanically. If I understood correctly, Death embodies the dragon's hunger, and Fate their regal ferocity. I think it could be interesting if you build upon tasting souls and incorporated it more in the Attainments.</div> </div> </div> </div>All good calls! I originally wanted to throw Prime in there since it was dragon-y in a way and I already had the Destiny Merit as a requirement, but I see now a better opportunity to play with its themes. The new Fate optional reqs should made them even more interesting as antagonists for players (especially the &quot;boss&quot; level one).<br /> <br /> Also, I totally blanked on the Duration factor thing, but I intended to have the Tasting bypass it. I added a new mechanical system for it \u2014 one which also enforces their lifestyle if one wishes to mechanically benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28963-wulfra","name":"Wulfra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}